## Q2. Use div for containers.

**Answer:**

The `<div>` element is used to group related HTML elements into a container.

Example:

```html
<div class="section">
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>I am a Computer Science student.</p>
</div>
```

## Q3. Give elements unique id and reusable class attributes.

**Answer:**

The `id` attribute uniquely identifies an element, while the `class` attribute can be reused for multiple elements.

Example:

```html
<div id="about" class="section">
    <h2>About Me</h2>
</div>

<div id="education" class="section">
    <h2>Education</h2>
</div>

<div id="skills" class="section">
    <h2>Skills</h2>
</div>
```

Here, every section has a unique `id`, while the class `section` is reused.

## Q4. Add a data-* custom attribute to any element.

**Answer:**

A `data-*` attribute stores custom information on an HTML element.

Example:

```html
<div id="skills" class="section" data-category="technical">
    <h2>My Skills</h2>
    <p>HTML, CSS, and Java.</p>
</div>
```

Here, `data-category="technical"` is a custom data attribute.

