## Q6. Organize the HTML code with proper indentation and meaningful names.

**Answer:**

Proper indentation makes HTML code easier to read and maintain. Meaningful names such as `about`, `education`, and `contact` help developers understand the purpose of each section.

Example:

```html
<div id="education" class="section">
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>B.Tech in Computer Science</p>
</div>
```

## Q7. Write the complete HTML code for the updated introduction page.

**Answer:**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Naman Pratap - Personal Introduction</title>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div id="header" class="section">
        <h1>Naman Pratap</h1>
        <p>B.Tech Computer Science Student</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- About Section -->
    <div id="about" class="section" data-category="personal">
        <h2>About Me</h2>
        <p id="intro-text">
            I am a B.Tech Computer Science student who enjoys learning
            web development, programming, and new technologies.
        </p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Education Section -->
    <div id="education" class="section">
        <h2>Education</h2>
        <p>I am pursuing B.Tech in Computer Science.</p>
        <p>My goal is to improve my technical knowledge and programming skills.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Skills Section -->
    <div id="skills" class="section" data-category="technical">
        <h2>My Skills</h2>
        <p>HTML</p>
        <p>CSS</p>
        <p>Java</p>
        <p>I am continuously learning new programming concepts.</p>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <!-- Contact Section -->
    <div id="contact" class="section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Email: student@example.com</p>
        <p>Feel free to contact me for academic projects.</p>
    </div>

</body>

</html>
```

## Q8. How do you run and verify the updated HTML page?

**Answer:**

